course: dictionary
lesson: 11055
title: Weedy: two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the words around the word: they are its context. «A weedy garden» is full of weeds, so here weedy describes a place that needs weeding.
explain: Read the clues. Informally, especially in Britain, weedy means thin and weak-looking, as in «weedy arms». Ask yourself: is the word describing a plant or a place, or a person?
explain: A description of a place can tell you about the people who live there. A weedy garden and a broken gate suggest that nobody cares for the house. The clues in the description give you the feeling the writer wants you to notice.
explain: Be kind with this word. Calling someone weedy to tease them is unkind, so describe what you see without hurting anyone.
fact: Weedy is an adjective: weedy, weedier, weediest.
fact: «Weedy» means full of weeds, as in «a weedy garden» or «weedy pond».
fact: Informally, especially in British English, «weedy» means thin and weak-looking, as in «weedy arms».
fact: A weedy patch needs weeding, so the word is useful in gardening and nature lessons.
fact: Calling a person weedy can be unkind, so do not use it to tease.
exercise: «The old shed stood in a weedy garden.» In this sentence, what does weedy mean? | *Full of weeds | Thin and weak-looking | Very quiet | Freshly painted
exercise: Ravi says, «He has weedy arms.» What does weedy mean here? | Covered in mud | Full of weeds | Very loud | *Thin and weak-looking
exercise: Which word fits a pond that is full of weeds? | *Weedy | Deep | Icy | Clean
test: A «weedy garden» and a «broken gate» suggest what about the house? | The house has just been painted | The family is very rich | The house is brand new | *Nobody cares for the house
test: What are the comparative and superlative forms of weedy? | weedies, weediest | *weedy, weedier, weediest | weedy, more weedy, most weedy | weeder, weedest
exam: Which sentence uses weedy to describe a person's looks? | «The gate was weedy and cracked.» | «The weedy garden needed a rake.» | *«Ben looked weedy beside the big boys.» | «The weedy pond was full of frogs.»
